-- title:
--   Descent of the cyclotomic determinant condition along a jointly injective pair
-- statement:
--   Let $P$, $A$, $B$ be commutative local rings and let $\pi_A : P \to A$ and $\pi_B : P \to B$ be ring homomorphisms which are local (non-units map to non-units), and suppose the pair is jointly injective: any $x \in P$ with $\pi_A x = 0$ and $\pi_B x = 0$ is zero. Let $\rho$ be a [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) over $P$, that is, a finite free $P$-module $V$ of rank $2$ together with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ (the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`) to $\mathrm{End}_P(V)$ satisfying the adic continuity condition: for every $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise satisfies $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}_P^n V$ for all $v$. Let $p$ be a natural number such that $(p : A)$ and $(p : B)$ are nilpotent, and assume that both base changes $B \otimes_P V$ along $\pi_A$ and along $\pi_B$, with $\sigma$ acting by the base change of $\rho(\sigma)$, satisfy `DetIsCyclotomic p`, namely: $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of the target, and for all $n$, all $\sigma$ and all $a \in \mathbb{N}$ such that $\sigma\mu = \mu^a$ for every $\mu$ with $\mu^{p^n} = 1$, the element $\det \rho(\sigma) - a$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^n$. Then $\rho$ itself satisfies `DetIsCyclotomic p` over $P$.
--
--   This is the descent, along a jointly injective pair of local homomorphisms, of the determinant condition occurring in Mazur's axioms for a deformation condition: the determinant of the representation agrees with the cyclotomic character modulo each power of $p$. It is used by the corresponding descent statements for the flat and ordinary local conditions, [`GaloisRepAdic.flatCondition_of_jointly_injective`](thm.html#GaloisRepAdic.flatCondition_of_jointly_injective), [`GaloisRep.ordinaryCondition_of_injective`](thm.html#GaloisRep.ordinaryCondition_of_injective) and [`GaloisRep.ordinaryCondition_of_jointly_injective`](thm.html#GaloisRep.ordinaryCondition_of_jointly_injective).
-- source:
